gest compression window","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Mineral de Pozos (day trip, Pueblo Mágico)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Ghost-mining town of ruined haciendas de beneficio, now an artist/mezcal Pueblo Mágico","bookable_category":"day-trip tour + transfer","tier":"comfort","source":"https://mexicotravel.blog/things-to-do-in-guanajuato-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-05)","timing":"October  — largest compression window","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Ghost-mining town of ruined haciendas de beneficio, now an artist/mezcal Pueblo Mágico","when":"October  — largest compression window","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Festival Internacional Cervantino","si_tag":"Live Entertainment","status":"future","hook":"Mexico''s largest performing-arts festival across theaters, alleys, plazas (Oct 7–25 2026)","bookable_category":"festival tickets + hotel package (long lead)","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.planetamericas.com/event/festival-internacional-cervantino (Accessed 2026-07-05)","timing":"October  — largest compression window","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"entertainment","blurb":"Mexico''s largest performing-arts festival across theaters, alleys, plazas (Oct 7–25 2026)","when":"October  — largest compression window","commission":"ticketing/event affiliate + hotel","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Teatro Juárez","si_tag":"Live Entertainment","status":"future","hook":"1873–1903 opera house, red-and-gold interior; year-round opera/ballet/concerts at reasonable prices","bookable_category":"performance tickets","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-guanajuato-city-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-05)","timing":"October  — largest compression window","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"entertainment","blurb":"1873–1903 opera house, red-and-gold interior; year-round opera/ballet/concerts at reasonable prices","when":"October  — largest compression window","commission":"ticketing/event affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"name":"Enchiladas mineras + plaza-café circuit","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Mining-town regional dish + café life of the Jardín de la Unión","bookable_category":"guided food walk","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-guanajuato-city-mexico/ (Accessed 2026-07-05)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culinary","blurb":"Mining-town regional dish + café life of the Jardín de la Unión","when":"year-round","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-05"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The southern-corridor highways, plus a steep city. The Level 3 driver is \"huachicol\" (oil-theft) violence along Hwy 45D and south — do not self-drive those routes. Otherwise the historic center is a compact walkable tourist zone; the practical caution is a very vertical, stepped city at **~2,000 m** (mild first-day altitude, sensible footwear, use the funicular).","source":"travel.state.gov / en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the Festival Cervantino, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"**Oct 7–25 in 2026** — and it sells out months ahead. It''s Mexico''s largest performing-arts festival and the single biggest compression window of the year; the booking curve builds ~4–6 months out at program/ticket release, so lock festival-and-hotel packages by late March / early April.","source":"planetamericas.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"entertainment"},{"q":"What are the must-see culture sites?","a":"The UNESCO historic core (inscribed 1988): the Museo de las Momias (111 mummified bodies), the Diego Rivera birth-house, the Alhóndiga de Granaditas, the belle-époque Teatro Juárez, and the El Pípila funicular for the 360° city panorama.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Guanajuato City romantic for couples?","a":"Strongly — it''s the bookable-today SI. The signature ritual is the **callejoneada**, a lantern-lit roving serenade led by costumed student musicians up alleys too narrow for cars, wine in hand, ending near the Callejón del Beso (kiss on the third step); pair it with the El Pípila funicular (~30 MXN) at sunset.","source":"en.wikipedia.org / mexicotravel.blog, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is there good food?","a":"Yes — Bajío regional cuisine in a UNESCO setting: the mining-town enchiladas mineras and the café life of the Jardín de la Unión, with the Guanajuato wine route nearby, best done as a guided food walk.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culinary"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Guanajuato City Travel Guide — UNESCO Mining Town, Callejones & Cervantino | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Mexico''s UNESCO silver-mining capital: colorful callejones, the Callejón del Beso, Teatro Juárez, the funicular to El Pípila, the Mummy Museum, Diego Rivera''s birth-house, the Festival Cervantino. Cristo Rey + Mineral de Pozos day trips. Bookable with mandatory L3 disclosure.","slug":"guanajuato-city-mexico","primary_keyword":"Guanajuato City travel guide","long_tail":["things to do in Guanajuato City 2026","is Guanajuato safe to visit 2026","Festival Cervantino 2026 dates","Callejón del Beso legend","Guanajuato Mummy Museum","funicular El Pípila","Cristo Rey del Cubilete day trip","Mineral de Pozos Pueblo Mágico","UNESCO Guanajuato hotels"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Guanajuato","¿es seguro viajar a Guanajuato?","Festival Cervantino fechas","Callejón del Beso leyenda","Museo de las Momias Guanajuato","funicular El Pípila","Cristo Rey del Cubilete","Mineral de Pozos pueblo mágico","hoteles boutique Guanajuato centro"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-05"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"entertainment","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Villa María Cristina","why_ultra":"City''s benchmark small-luxury; Small Luxury Hotels member; 13 suites (Roche-Bobois, marble baths, B&O); Roman-style spa; near historic center","earning":"on application / SLH via host / Fora lane","mor":true,"tier":"luxury-boutique"},{"name":"1850 Hotel Boutique","why_ultra":"Historic-center design boutique with domed stained-glass skylight; walkable to Teatro Juárez + Jardín","earning":"on application / host program","mor":true,"tier":"premier-luxury-boutique"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-05","hero":{"query":"Guanajuato City, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":21.019,"lng":-101.2574}}'::jsonb, 44),
  ('guatemala-city-guatemala', '10S', 'Guatemala City', 'Guatemala', 'The first breath of Guatemala', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Guatemala', '{"culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["La Aurora (GUA/MGGT) is Guatemala''s primary international gateway, 4th-busiest in Central America, 4,919,850 pax in 2024, direct US links via AA/UA/DL + Avianca hub.","City runs a numbered-zone system; traveler-relevant zones are Zone 1 (historic core), Zone 10 ''Zona Viva'' (hotels/dining/museums), Zone 13 (airport + museum row).","Antigua Guatemala is ~45–60 min (~40–45 km) by road; GC functions primarily as a transfer point to Antigua/Atitlán/Tikal.","Museum cluster is first-rate: Museo Popol Vuh (best pre-Hispanic/colonial art) + Museo Ixchel (~8,000 textiles, 180+ communities), both on the UFM campus in Zone 10.","Safety is zone-specific: US Level 3; Zone 18 + Villa Nueva are Level 4 ''Do Not Travel''; Zones 10/14, Zone 1 core, and Cayalá (Zone 16, safest) are where visitors stay."],"safety":{"emergency":"Police 110 · Fire/Ambulance 122 (also 123) · Red Cross 125 · PROATUR tourist assistance 1500 (from abroad +502 2290 2810)","hospital":"Hospital Herrera Llerandi (6a. Avenida 8-71, Zona 10; +502 2384-5959) — Forbes-recognized best hospital in Guatemala, CAP-accredited; Centro Médico + Hospital Universitario tier; GC is the national medical + medevac hub","book_enabled":true,"book_enabled_note":"BOOK WITH WARNING (Four-Bin v3) — founder-blessed as bookable-with-warning; booking enabled with mandatory full-advisory disclosure","l3_disclosure":true,"in_city_nogo":"Zone 18 + Villa Nueva","state_dept_carveout":"airport Zone 13 + Zona Viva Zones 10/14 + Zone 1 historic safe; NEVER route to Zone 18 or Villa Nueva","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"La Aurora International Airport (GUA / MGGT)","urban_crime":"vetted taxi/Uber only, no street-hailing; no night walking in unfamiliar zones","health":"dengue precautions; bottled water only","water":"bottled only"},"timing":{"demand_type":"derivative","curve_driver":"onward anchors (Antigua/Atitlán/Tikal) + country dry season Nov–Mar","inflection":"early-to-mid October","peak":"November–March + Semana Santa (late Mar / Apr)","shoulder_green":"May–October (rainy season)","booking_lead":"2–4 months dry season; 5–6+ months Semana Santa","events":["Semana Santa / Holy Week (movable, late Mar / Apr)"],"fire_date":"2026-09-20","fire_date_note":"gateway-booking window = curve-start (~mid-Oct) minus 1–2 weeks; lock GC beds + vetted transfers ahead of anchor demand. Semana Santa sub-fire Oct–Nov. Sharpen on live gateway tracking.","confidence":"medium-derived"},"jewels":[{"name":"Museo Popol Vuh","si_tag":"culture","zone":"10 (UFM)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universidad_Francisco_Marroqu%C3%ADn (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"\"one of the best collections of pre-Hispanic and colonial art in the country.\"","si":"culture","blurb":"\"one of the best collections of pre-Hispanic and colonial art in the country.\"","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"admission non-commissionable → bundle into commissioned DMC city tour","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Museo Ixchel del Traje Indígena","si_tag":"culture","zone":"10 (UFM)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://museoixchel.org/en/museo-ixchel-english/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"~8,000 textile pieces from 180+ Indigenous communities; huipiles, cortes, ceremonial garments; open Mon–Fri 9–5, Sat 9–1","si":"culture","blurb":"~8,000 textile pieces from 180+ Indigenous communities; huipiles, cortes, ceremonial garments; open Mon–Fri 9–5, Sat 9–1","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"admission non-commissionable → guided textile tour + Antigua/Atitlán artisan retail linkage","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Museo Nacional de Arqueología y Etnología","si_tag":"culture","zone":"13","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guatemala_City (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"bundle into DMC city tour","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Zone 1 Historic Center (Palacio Nacional, Cathedral, Mercado Central)","si_tag":"culture","zone":"1","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guatemala_City (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the founding civic core: National Palace, Cathedral, and the underground artisan market","si":"culture","blurb":"the founding civic core: National Palace, Cathedral, and the underground artisan market","when":"year-round","commission":"commissioned daytime historic-center walking tour via DMC","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Paseo Cayalá / Ciudad Cayalá","si_tag":"Lifestyle/Dining","zone":"16","tier":"comfort","source":"https://livinginguatemala.com/neighborhoods/zona-16-cayala/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Lifestyle/Dining","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"non-bookable district → hotel night + DMC evening transfer","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Zona Viva dining","si_tag":"Lifestyle/Dining","zone":"10","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guatemala_City (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Lifestyle/Dining","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"hotel-package upsell","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Antigua Guatemala transfer/day-trip","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage / Adventure","zone":"onward (~45 min)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/articles/best-time-to-visit-guatemala (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"colonial UNESCO city; the real reason GC exists as a gateway","si":"Culture & Heritage / Adventure","blurb":"colonial UNESCO city; the real reason GC exists as a gateway","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"commissioned DMC transfer + Antigua land package (primary revenue move)","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Pacaya Volcano day-trip","si_tag":"adventure","zone":"onward (~1.5–2 hr)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.martsam.com/ (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"November–March + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","when":"November–March + Semana Santa","commission":"commissioned DMC guided excursion","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"La Aurora Zoo","si_tag":"Family/Layover","zone":"13","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guatemala_City (Accessed 2026-07-06)","si":"Family/Layover","commission":"non-commissionable admission; long-layover add-on","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"Should I stay in Guatemala City or head straight to Antigua?","a":"Treat Guatemala City as a 1–2-night stopover, not a leisure anchor. It''s the international gateway — La Aurora (Central America''s 4th-busiest, 4,919,850 pax in 2024) sits in Zone 13, ~45–60 minutes (~40–45 km) from Antigua — so most travelers rest a night, then road out to the country''s true anchors.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":null},{"q":"Is Guatemala City worth a stop for museums?","a":"Yes, for a half-day. The museum cluster is genuinely first-rate: Museo Popol Vuh holds one of the country''s best pre-Hispanic and colonial-art collections, and Museo Ixchel holds ~8,000 textile pieces from 180+ Indigenous communities, both on the UFM campus in the safe Zone 10.","source":"museoixchel.org, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How do I get from the airport safely?","a":"Use arranged or vetted transport, or Uber — never a street-hailed taxi. Move from La Aurora (Zone 13) to Zone 10/14 lodging on pre-arranged transport, avoid walking at night in unfamiliar zones, and ride the onward Antigua/Atitlán/Tikal handoff on a vetted shuttle or the DMC''s own transport.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Guatemala City Travel Guide — La Aurora Gateway, Zona Viva & Safe-Zone Stopover | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Accurate guide to Guatemala City as the international gateway (GUA) to Antigua, Atitlán & Tikal — Zona Viva stays, museum cluster, safety zones, Level 3 route-around.","search_language":["en","es-GT"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Ciudad de Guatemala","Zona Viva hoteles","escala Guatemala City","Museo Ixchel Zona 10","traslado aeropuerto La Aurora a Antigua","zonas seguras Ciudad de Guatemala"],"long_tail_en":["Guatemala City stopover before Antigua","is Guatemala City safe Zona Viva Zone 10","La Aurora airport to Antigua transfer","best hotels Zona Viva Guatemala City","Guatemala travel advisory Zone 18 Villa Nueva"],"hreflang":["en","es-GT"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["Culture & Heritage (future)"],"ultra":[{"property":"Westin Camino Real (Zone 10)","play":"premier gateway night","channel":"Fora/Virtuoso consortia; else GDS commissioned","mor":"Fora advisor","tier":"premier"},{"property":"InterContinental Guatemala (Zone 10)","play":"business-luxury gateway","channel":"IHG consortia / Fora","mor":"Fora/consortia","tier":"premier"},{"property":"Barceló Guatemala City (Zone 10)","play":"upper premier gateway","channel":"consortia / GDS","mor":"consortia","tier":"premier"},{"property":"Hyatt Centric (Zone 10)","play":"lifestyle premier gateway","channel":"Hyatt Privé / Fora","mor":"Fora/Privé","tier":"premier"},{"property":"Antigua boutique-colonial base (REDIRECT)","play":"the true ultra stay — GC is transit","channel":"Fora/Virtuoso Antigua portfolio","mor":"Fora advisor","tier":"ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Guatemala City, Guatemala"},"geo":{"lat":14.6349,"lng":-90.5069}}'::jsonb, 45),
