,"tier":"comfort","source":"https://iguazufalls.com/tours-and-activities/gran-aventura-activity/","hook":"the adrenaline jewel: 4×4 jungle trail to Puerto Macuco, then a 6 km semi-rigid run into the San Martín falls \"baptism of the mists.\"","si":"expedition","blurb":"the adrenaline jewel: 4×4 jungle trail to Puerto Macuco, then a 6 km semi-rigid run into the San Martín falls \"baptism of the mists.\"","commission":"in-park concession (largely non-commissionable) — package via DMC / frame via activity affiliate"},{"name":"Full-Moon Walk (Paseos de Luna Llena)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://iguazufalls.com/tours-and-activities/full-moon-walk-tour/","hook":"5 nights a month only, timed to the full moon: welcome drink + Guaraní music, Eco-Train through the night jungle to the Throat catwalk","si":"expedition","blurb":"5 nights a month only, timed to the full moon: welcome drink + Guaraní music, Eco-Train through the night jungle to the Throat catwalk","commission":"guided-only ticket via activity affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"Sunrise with in-park hotel (Gran Meliá privilege)","si_tag":"GEA/RHN","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.jacadatravel.com/latin-america/argentina/iguazu-falls/accommodation/melia-iguazu/","si":"GEA/RHN","commission":"in-park hotel booking (ultra lane)"},{"name":"Macuco jungle trail","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"http://www.iguazujungle.com/eng/web2/","hook":"the park''s longer forest walk to a hidden waterfall; coatis, toucans, capuchins, butterflies","si":"expedition","blurb":"the park''s longer forest walk to a hidden waterfall; coatis, toucans, capuchins, butterflies","commission":"self-guided or guided via in-park operator + DMC"},{"name":"Güirá Oga wildlife refuge","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.welcomeargentina.com/puertoiguazu/lodge-awasi-iguazu_i.html","hook":"\"bird house\" in Guaraní; a rescue-and-rehab centre for trafficked/injured native fauna just outside Puerto Iguazú","si":"expedition","blurb":"\"bird house\" in Guaraní; a rescue-and-rehab centre for trafficked/injured native fauna just outside Puerto Iguazú","commission":"activity affiliate + DMC add-on"},{"name":"Brazilian-side panorama day-trip","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://sayhueque.com/our-trips/iguazu-falls/","hook":"cross to Parque Nacional do Iguaçu for the whole-system framed view Argentina can''t give you; passport-required border crossing, ~3–4 hr","si":"culture","blurb":"cross to Parque Nacional do Iguaçu for the whole-system framed view Argentina can''t give you; passport-required border crossing, ~3–4 hr","commission":"DMC/guided transfer + activity affiliate (cross-ref Brazil-side dossier)"},{"name":"San Ignacio Miní (UNESCO Jesuit-Guaraní mission)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/275/","hook":"the roofless red-sandstone cathedral of a 1610 Jesuit reduction, UNESCO-listed 1984, ~300 km south toward Posadas","si":"culture","blurb":"the roofless red-sandstone cathedral of a 1610 Jesuit reduction, UNESCO-listed 1984, ~300 km south toward Posadas","commission":"DMC / guided excursion + activity affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the best plan for a day at Iguazú Falls?","a":"Run the Devil''s Throat first at the 08:00 park opening, then work back through the Upper and Lower Circuits. The park opens 08:00 and closes 18:00 with last falls access around 16:30, and starting at the Garganta station gives the best rainbow light and thinnest crowds; budget 5–6 hours minimum for all three circuits plus the Eco-Train.","source":"iguazufalls-tickets.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Iguazú Falls?","a":"March–April and August–September are the sweet spot, because they balance strong water flow with comfortable 20–30 °C temperatures and manageable crowds. December–February brings maximum flow but heat above 35 °C and peak crowds, while May is a quiet sleeper month with autumn flow and room rates 30–40% below the Dec–Feb peak.","source":"iguazutickets.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where should honeymooners stay at Iguazú?","a":"The two scarce in-jewel beds are the play: Awasi Iguazú (Relais & Châteaux, 14 stilted villas with a private guide and 4×4 each) and the Gran Meliá Iguazú, the only hotel inside the Argentine park. Both are near-zero on bedbanks and contract direct or via DMC, so book Awasi or an in-park falls-view room 6–12 months ahead.","source":"relaischateaux.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Should I visit the Brazilian side too — and what else is nearby?","a":"Yes if time allows: Argentina holds ~80% of the falls and the immersion, while Brazil''s single panoramic boardwalk delivers the whole-system view as a passport-required border day-trip. South toward Posadas, the roofless red-sandstone cathedral of San Ignacio Miní (UNESCO-listed 1984) rounds out a cultural-heritage circuit.","source":"sayhueque.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Iguazú?","a":"Health and weather, not crime. Misiones province carries a CDC yellow-fever vaccination recommendation and a real dengue risk, so pack DEET and get a pre-travel vaccination consult; the catwalks are permanently misted and slippery, and extreme rainfall can close the Devil''s Throat catwalk on river surge.","source":"wwwnc.cdc.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Gran Aventura speedboat dangerous?","a":"It is operator-run and low-risk with the rules followed, but not trivial. A life jacket is mandatory and a safety briefing is given before the 6 km run into the San Martín falls; jacket-quality reviews are mixed, so non-swimmers should weigh the run, everyone gets thoroughly soaked, and the trip is river-level-dependent and cancels in high water.","source":"iguazufalls.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Iguazú Falls, Argentine Side: Devil''s Throat, the Circuits & Gran Aventura Boat | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Stand over the Devil''s Throat, walk the Upper and Lower Circuits, run the Gran Aventura boat under the falls, and stay inside the national park — the complete guide to the Argentine side of Iguazú.","long_tail_en":["iguazu falls argentine side guide","garganta del diablo devil''s throat iguazu","iguazu upper and lower circuits","gran aventura boat ride iguazu","iguazu falls full moon walk","best time to visit iguazu falls","gran melia iguazu in-park hotel","awasi iguazu relais chateaux","iguazu argentina vs brazil side","san ignacio mini jesuit ruins"],"search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["Cataratas del Iguazú","Garganta del Diablo","Gran Aventura Iguazú","circuito superior e inferior Iguazú","Tren Ecológico de la Selva","paseo de luna llena Cataratas","San Ignacio Miní ruinas","qué hacer en Puerto Iguazú"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Iguazú Falls (Argentine Side)"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Awasi Iguazu","type":"Relais & Chateaux all-inclusive villa lodge","location":"Misiones jungle, ~20 min from falls","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora advisor commission + amenities","mor":"AOR/advisor","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Gran Melia Iguazu","type":"in-park hotel (only one, Argentine side)","location":"inside Iguazu National Park","earning":"advisor/DMC commission + RedLevel upsell","mor":"AOR/advisor/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Loi Suites Iguazu","type":"upscale jungle-river resort","location":"Iryapu reserve, ~10 min from Puerto Iguazu","earning":"advisor/DMC commission","mor":"AOR/DMC","tier":"luxury"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Iguazú Falls (Argentine Side), Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-25.6953,"lng":-54.4367}}'::jsonb, 49)
