the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"gray-whale HARD window ~mid-Jan-mid-Mar (calving lagoon)","second_peak":"sardine run / striped-marlin bait ball, mid-Oct-Dec","shoulder":"late Dec-early Jan (arrival), late Mar-Apr (tail-end)","green":"May-Sep (off-season, hot, hurricane-exposed)","booking_window_lead_time":"6-12 months (tiny whale-camp capacity, both windows sell out early)","out_of_season_fill":"minimal; sport fishing + birding fill edges","holiday_event_peaks":["US/Canada winter escape overlaps gray-whale peak"],"campaign_start_trigger":"gray-whale 9-12 months out; marlin/sardine-run by mid-summer for Oct-Dec"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Gray-whale calving-lagoon encounter","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator; net-rate red","name":"Barrier-island whale-camp overnight","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"essential","commission":"operator","name":"Mangrove / birding skiff","si":"expedition"},{"si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Snorkel-with-striped-marlin bait ball (sardine run)","si":"ocean"},{"si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"luxury","commission":"operator/wholesale","name":"Striped-marlin liveaboard (Nautilus)","si":"ocean"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is gray-whale season in Magdalena Bay?","a":"The hard window is roughly mid-January to mid-March, when mothers and calves fill the calving lagoon; whales arrive late Dec–early Jan and linger to April. Mag Bay''s grays are famously \"friendly,\" often approaching the pangas — book the tiny whale-camp capacity 6–12 months ahead.","source":"seakayakadventures.com / randomtrip.net, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I snorkel the striped-marlin bait balls?","a":"Yes, from about mid-October to December — but it''s an advanced open-water activity. You''re offshore in current among fast-moving marlin and sea lions driving sardines to the surface, so it''s for confident, fit snorkelers and freedivers with specialist operators only.","source":"magdalenabaywhales.com / divernet.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Where do I stay — are there resorts?","a":"No resorts — the accurate options are a barrier-island whale camp (glamping, 1–7 nights, ~$650+ for a 1-night all-in) or basic hotels in Puerto San Carlos and López Mateos. The camp is part of the experience: whales from shore, and nothing between you and the lagoon.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is the bait-ball snorkel dangerous?","a":"It is not a beginner activity. The sardine run happens offshore in current among fast predators, so go only with specialist operators, follow the guide''s positioning rules and never touch the wildlife; if you dive elsewhere in Baja, the nearest chambers are La Paz and Cabo San Lucas with 18–24 h no-fly.","source":"divernet.com / sssnetwork.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Magdalena Bay — Gray-Whale Lagoon & Striped-Marlin Sardine Run | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Magdalena Bay, Baja California Sur: gray-whale calving lagoon (Jan-Mar) and the striped-marlin bait-ball sardine run (Oct-Dec). Whale-camp stays, seasons, safe-panga guidance.","primary_keywords":["Magdalena Bay whale watching","gray whale Magdalena Bay","striped marlin bait ball","Baja sardine run"],"long_tail":["gray whale season Magdalena Bay 2026","snorkel with striped marlin Baja","Magdalena Bay whale camp","Puerto San Carlos whale watching","how to get to Magdalena Bay from Los Cabos"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["ballena gris Bahia Magdalena","avistamiento de ballenas Puerto San Carlos","marlin rayado Bahia Magdalena","corrida de la sardina Baja","campamento de ballenas Bahia Magdalena"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristAttraction","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","ocean"],"ultra":[{"what":"National Geographic / Lindblad expedition cruise to Magdalena Bay (sea-based); or Los Cabos/East Cape ultra property as pre/post base","why_ultra":"small-ship expedition w/ naturalists is the only refined product on the bay; no land ultra exists here (nearest = Los Cabos/East Cape 3.5-6 h away)","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso; expedition-cruise lines carry advisor commission","virtuoso_value_add":"shipboard credit/expedition perks via preferred programs, or resort credit at Los Cabos base","mor":"resale via host-Virtuoso / cruise-wholesale only; Magdalena Bay lodging itself is NOT ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Magdalena Bay, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":24.6167,"lng":-112.1}}'::jsonb, 61)
